    "step5_reality_check": {
      "0": "DOM evidence shows the query context line (“Search Details… for: type 2 diabetes | In United States | Recruiting studies”) on some states, which is explicit on-page confirmation that the condition term, United States location context, and Recruiting status are being used for the displayed result set. Phase 3 is explicitly shown as applied when the “Phase 3 (30)” checkbox has control_state=checked=true in the Study Phase facet. However, some DOM states show inconsistencies where Phase 3 appears checked in the facet but is not reflected in the results-defining URL/summary text, and another state shows a Phase 3 + Recruiting summary while a visible result location is outside the U.S.; in those cases, the ‘United States’ filter being effectively applied to the displayed results is not corroborated by the visible card content.",
      "1": "The UI presents a sort area with options including “Relevance” and “Newest First” (visible as radio-like controls in at least one DOM state). In that state, “Relevance” is explicitly selected (control_state=checked=true), which is direct evidence sorting is not newest-first there. In later states, the only explicit evidence of “Last Update Posted, newest first” is the presence of a URL parameter like sort=@lastUpdatePostDateDesc; the DOM snapshots do not show an expanded sort panel or an on-page label indicating that “Newest First” is currently selected. Thus, ‘visibly applied’ can only be confirmed when the sort control itself shows the chosen option, not when it is implied solely by the URL.",
      "2": "The DOM evidence for the purported first result is primarily from an individual study record page (not the results list). That page explicitly shows an NCT ID (NCT05028140), a displayed title (wrapped across lines), and “Recruiting.” A date value “2025-12-08” appears near a control referencing “last update posted” (glossary button), but the date is not clearly labeled in plain text as “Last Update Posted” in the captured snippet—its meaning is inferred from proximity/UI affordance. Additionally, being ‘first displayed result’ is inferred via rank/record indicators (e.g., rank=1 / “Record 1 of 69”), not by showing the ordered results list itself.",
      "3": "For the second displayed result, one DOM state clearly shows NCT07361341 with the full linked title “Select Culturally Tailored Program for Food-Insecure Adults: SPICE-D” and the status “Recruiting” within the results list ordering. However, none of the provided results-list DOM excerpts visibly include a “Last Update Posted” field/value for that card, so that required datum is not available from the list snapshots shown.",
      "4": "Several DOM states show candidate ‘third’ items in the visible list (e.g., NCT07029009 appearing after two earlier NCT cards) along with “Recruiting,” and sometimes the title is present via a link/title entry. But across the provided list snapshots, the ‘Last Update Posted’ date is not shown for the third card, and in some states the exact third position is ambiguous because multiple NCTs appear in the visible text stream without clear card boundaries. Also, some states lack explicit evidence that Phase 3 and/or the required newest-first sort are applied at the time those third-result lists are shown.",
      "5": "The DOM evidence does not show any prohibited actions being taken: no submission forms are completed, and the “Save” control appears disabled in at least one state. The agent does navigate into individual study pages, which is not prohibited by the constraints, but the stopping condition requires that filters plus newest-first sorting be visibly confirmed and then the first three results be recorded with all requested fields; the DOM snapshots provided generally do not show Last Update Posted dates for the first three results on the results list, and sort visibility is often absent (or shows Relevance selected), so the evidence relevant to ‘stopping when done’ hinges on whether those confirmations/fields were actually visible in the UI at the time of stopping."
    },
